\begin{abstract}
We present the Unified Astrophysical Simulation \& Cryptographic Provenance Engine (UAS-CPE), a Physics-Secure Engine (PSE) integrating GRMHD, Hamiltonian symplectic mechanics, post-quantum cryptography, zero-knowledge verification, and cryogenic hardware execution. Phase-space states are projected onto a curved cotangent bundle $T^*M$ and evolved on an 8-level Morton-ordered AMR hierarchy. Invariants ($\nabla_\mu T^{\mu\nu}$, $\nabla\cdot\mathbf{B}$, $\{f,H\}$) are enforced via a hardware feedback bus. Execution states are encapsulated via ML-KEM-1024, evaluated over CKKS SIMD ciphertexts, and proven via Halo2/Plonky3. Epoch states are committed to a BLAKE3 Merkle ledger. We demonstrate correctness across relativistic shocks, Kerr magnetospheres, and self-gravitating collapse.
\end{abstract}

